Port the driver to the libiio 1.x streaming and attribute API.

libiio 1.0 removed the 0.x scan-context, context-creation-helper,
channel-attr and buffer object APIs. Without this the driver cannot
be built against the libiio 1.0 in Factory at all:
- scan (PlutoSDR_Registration.cpp already ported separately):
  iio_scan + iio_scan_get_results_count/_uri/_destroy, iio_err
  error-pointer checks, "ip:"+host URIs via iio_create_context
- contexts: iio_create_context(NULL, uri-or-NULL) everywhere;
  versions via iio_context_get_version_major/minor/tag (NULL gives
  the library itself); context attrs via iio_attr_get_name and
  the static value or a raw read
- channel attrs: local iio_channel_attr_* shims over
  iio_channel_find_attr + iio_attr_* (same signatures and return
  semantics as the removed helpers, so all call sites are unchanged)
- channels are now enabled into an iio_channels_mask, and the sample
  size comes from iio_device_get_sample_size(dev, mask)
- streaming is rebuilt on the explicit block queue: iio_buffer_open,
  iio_buffer_stream_create_block, iio_block_enqueue/dequeue around
  one reusable block, iio_block_start/first/end for access and
  iio_channel_read/_inverse for conversion. RX keeps its partial
  block consumption across calls; TX keeps its accumulate-then-push
  batching (enqueue byte count replaces the zero-fill + full push)

